# How The Web Works Module | TryHackMe

## Overview
This module breaks down the building blocks of the World Wide Web, explaining the technical processes that occur from typing a URL to viewing a webpage. Essential for web application security.

### Topics Covered:
- **DNS in Detail**: How domain names resolve to IP addresses
- **HTTP in Detail**: Client-server communication via HTTP protocol
- **How Websites Work**: Web architecture from a developer and attacker perspective
- **Putting it all together**: End-to-end flow of web requests

### Skills Gained:
- Understanding DNS resolution and common DNS attacks
- HTTP methods, headers, status codes, and request/response cycle
- How browsers render websites: HTML, CSS, JS
- The complete lifecycle of a web request
- Foundation for Web Exploitation and Bug Bounty

> Platform: TryHackMe | Category: Web Fundamentals / Offensive Security
